<description>
  <page>
    <p><strong style="color:#3b82f6">Introduction to Chemistry</strong></p>
    <p>Chemistry is the scientific study of matter, its properties, and how substances interact, combine, and change.</p>
    
    <table border="1">
      <tr>
        <th style="color:#3b82f6">Element</th>
        <th style="color:#3b82f6">Symbol</th>
        <th style="color:#3b82f6">Atomic Number</th>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Hydrogen</td>
        <td>H</td>
        <td>1</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Carbon</td>
        <td>C</td>
        <td>6</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Oxygen</td>
        <td>O</td>
        <td>8</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Nitrogen</td>
        <td>N</td>
        <td>7</td>
      </tr>
    </table>
    
    <p>Chemistry helps us understand everything from cooking to medicine to environmental science.</p>
    <p>🔹 More Info: <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=chemistry+basics" target="_blank">Chemistry Fundamentals</a></p>
  </page>

  <page>
    <p><strong style="color:#10b981">The Water Molecule</strong></p>
    <p>Water (H₂O) is essential for life. Each molecule consists of two hydrogen atoms bonded to one oxygen atom.</p>
    
    <svg width="400" height="300">
      <!-- Oxygen atom -->
      <circle cx="200" cy="150" r="40" fill="#ef4444" stroke="#991b1b" stroke-width="3"/>
      <text x="190" y="160" font-size="24" fill="white" font-weight="bold">O</text>
      
      <!-- Hydrogen atoms -->
      <circle cx="120" cy="100" r="25" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="3"/>
      <text x="113" y="110" font-size="20" fill="#1f2937" font-weight="bold">H</text>
      
      <circle cx="280" cy="100" r="25" fill="#ffffff" stroke="#6b7280" stroke-width="3"/>
      <text x="273" y="110" font-size="20" fill="#1f2937" font-weight="bold">H</text>
      
      <!-- Bonds -->
      <line x1="140" y1="110" x2="180" y2="135" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="4"/>
      <line x1="260" y1="110" x2="220" y2="135" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="4"/>
      
      <!-- Bond angle -->
      <text x="160" y="200" font-size="18" fill="#f59e0b" font-weight="bold">104.5°</text>
    </svg>
    
    <p>The bent molecular geometry and polar nature make water an excellent solvent.</p>
    
    <ul>
      <li>Polar covalent bonds</li>
      <li>Bent shape (104.5° angle)</li>
      <li>Strong hydrogen bonding</li>
      <li>Universal solvent properties</li>
    </ul>
    
    <p>🔹 More Info: <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=water+molecule+structure" target="_blank">Water Molecule Structure</a></p>
  </page>

  <page>
    <p><strong style="color:#f59e0b">Chemical Reactions</strong></p>
    <p>Chemical reactions transform reactants into products. Here's the combustion of methane:</p>
    
    <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
      <mrow>
        <msub><mi>CH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub>
        <mo>+</mo>
        <mn>2</mn>
        <msub><mi>O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub>
        <mo>→</mo>
        <msub><mi>CO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub>
        <mo>+</mo>
        <mn>2</mn>
        <msub><mi>H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub>
        <mi>O</mi>
      </mrow>
    </math>
    
    <p><strong style="color:#ef4444">Steps to Balance Equations:</strong></p>
    <ol>
      <li>Write the unbalanced equation</li>
      <li>Count atoms of each element</li>
      <li>Add coefficients to balance</li>
      <li>Check that all atoms balance</li>
      <li>Ensure coefficients are in lowest terms</li>
    </ol>
    
    <table border="1">
      <tr>
        <th style="color:#f59e0b">Reaction Type</th>
        <th style="color:#f59e0b">Example</th>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Synthesis</td>
        <td>A + B → AB</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Decomposition</td>
        <td>AB → A + B</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Combustion</td>
        <td>Fuel + O₂ → CO₂ + H₂O</td>
      </tr>
    </table>
    
    <p>🔹 More Info: <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=chemical+reactions+types" target="_blank">Types of Chemical Reactions</a></p>
  </page>

  <page>
    <p><strong style="color:#8b5cf6">The Periodic Table</strong></p>
    <p>The periodic table organizes all known chemical elements by atomic number and properties.</p>
    
    <svg width="500" height="300">
      <!-- Simplified periodic table -->
      <rect x="20" y="20" width="60" height="60" fill="#fde68a" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="2"/>
      <text x="50" y="50" text-anchor="middle" font-size="16" font-weight="bold">H</text>
      <text x="50" y="70" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12">1</text>
      
      <rect x="440" y="20" width="60" height="60" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="2"/>
      <text x="470" y="50" text-anchor="middle" font-size="16" font-weight="bold">He</text>
      <text x="470" y="70" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12">2</text>
      
      <rect x="20" y="100" width="60" height="60" fill="#fde68a" stroke="#f59e0b" stroke-width="2"/>
      <text x="50" y="130" text-anchor="middle" font-size="16" font-weight="bold">Li</text>
      <text x="50" y="150" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12">3</text>
      
      <rect x="380" y="100" width="60" height="60" fill="#dbeafe" stroke="#3b82f6" stroke-width="2"/>
      <text x="410" y="130" text-anchor="middle" font-size="16" font-weight="bold">Ne</text>
      <text x="410" y="150" text-anchor="middle" font-size="12">10</text>
      
      <text x="20" y="220" font-size="14" fill="#f59e0b">● Metals</text>
      <text x="120" y="220" font-size="14" fill="#3b82f6">● Non-metals</text>
    </svg>
    
    <p><strong style="color:#10b981">Key Trends:</strong></p>
    <ul>
      <li>Atomic radius decreases left to right</li>
      <li>Ionization energy increases left to right</li>
      <li>Electronegativity increases toward fluorine</li>
      <li>Metallic character decreases left to right</li>
    </ul>
    
    <p>🔹 More Info: <a href="https://www.google.com/search?q=periodic+table+trends" target="_blank">Periodic Table Trends</a></p>
  </page>
</description>
